    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 6 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be left with the lowest pip total when the hand ends, either by going out or by blocked play.',
      'Turn-flow example: Play proceeds on a single train, adding one matching tile to either open end. In hands with undealt center tiles, one center tile is exposed to start the line. In 4-player 7-tile play, the double blank 0-0 starts the first hand and later hands begin with a double from the previous winner side. A blocked player usually discards one dead tile face down; some tables use pass-only handling.',
      'Scoring example: At hand end, each player totals pips on all unplayed tiles, including dead tiles if used. Lowest total wins the hand. Winner is the player with least points; ties are broken by lowest single tile, then lowest end value..',
